      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "https://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/feedback-please-add-grab-state-to-animator-parametersboth-handsanimator-paramete\nI requested to add visibility of the grab state to the common avatar PARAMETER. I feel it would be quite important to be able to send whether it is in a grab state or not for application in avatar dynamics.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-06T22:31:09.445Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently if you want to detect if a contact is grabbed, you have to check for a gesture value and the contact value. However this isn't very compatible with Valve Index users (also who may have gestures off). This also requires extra logic states to first detect intersection and then the gesture to prevent things magneting to an already closed hand, etc.\nIt's almost easier to just use a physbone, and use it to detect the grab, but this has a needless performance and rating impact since it simulates physics that are then just being ignored.\nIt would be really nice if contacts had a \"Grab\" mode that would provide a controller-agnostic way of detecting a grab using the grab sphere.",
